https://github.com/ruby/ruby/pull/19020: nested bounded repeats overflow the int product
that decides whether to unroll a repeat inline, so Regexp.new("(?:.{90000,}){90000}")
starts unrolling an enormous program and never returns. Ruby only acts on a signal once
the C call returns, so SIGTERM doesn't stop it either. The product is compared by
division instead, and the program size is capped as it's emitted.

The error codes are one lower than upstream's (-225 to -227, not -224 to -226): this
Onigmo already spends -224 on ONIGERR_TOO_MANY_CAPTURE_GROUPS. Ruby only ever sees the
message, never the number.

